  "description": "The 747-400BCF version of National's scheme: silver-white with 'NATIONAL' in big royal-blue heavy italic capitals over the forward main deck behind (left) or ahead of (right) a blue italic block, 'www.nationalairlines.com' small underneath, a thin red line curving up from the wing root to the crown, and two thin wavy blue lines running from above the wing back and up into the fin's root. On the fin three blue bands split by white lines sweep up to the trailing edge, a white strip along the leading edge. White engines, blue winglets.",
