  "notes": "Worn by the 747-400BCF N729CA (tagged in airframes/NCR.json); which of National's other converted 747s wear it isn't settled by 2024-2026 Commons photos. Fitted on N729CA 2022-05-10 (right, from below, no doors in view): along the fuselage the title runs x 0.108-0.374, the block 0.374-0.436, the lines leave the fuselage side pointed at x 0.54 (lower) and 0.58 (upper), under the wing. Heights: that fit put the title about 0.35 of the half-height lower than the level -400F photo does; the two schemes' titles are taken to sit alike, so the lines' heights here are shifted by the same amount (low certainty). The red line and the fin's three bands and two white lines are the -400F's, measured on N537CA (2026): N729CA's fin shows the same banding in 2022 and 2026 without the red line along the top; the red line over the wing is on N729CA in 2026 (both sides) and hidden by the wing in the 2022 photo. No logo after the block in the 2026 photos. Winglets blue with thin white lines (not drawn), inner faces unseen. Colours by eye.",
  "history": "New in the LAX round (2026-11-20)."
